Subject: [PATCH] Treat expired synchronized notifications as normal cancellation

Qt removes pending posted events when their receiver is destroyed. Events
copied into Krita's private postponed queue cannot be removed by QObject's
cleanup, but their QPointer is cleared and already prevents delivery.

Saving through a nested event loop can destroy the background document and
its shape-controller connections before the outer GUI event returns. Treat
these expired notifications as cancelled without reporting a warning.
Keep the lifetime guard and the delivery order of surviving receivers.

Related upstream issue: https://bugs.kde.org/show_bug.cgi?id=488226
The same diagnostic is reported during scripted save/close on desktop.
This local change retains the existing cancellation guard.

diff --git a/libs/ui/KisApplication.cpp b/libs/ui/KisApplication.cpp
--- a/libs/ui/KisApplication.cpp
+++ b/libs/ui/KisApplication.cpp
@@ -975,8 +975,9 @@
         KisSynchronizedConnectionEvent typedEvent = info.postponedSynchronizationEvents.front();
         info.postponedSynchronizationEvents.pop();
 
+        // Like Qt's posted events, notifications in this private queue are
+        // cancelled when their receiver is destroyed during a nested event loop.
         if (!typedEvent.destination) {
-            qWarning() << "WARNING: the destination object of KisSynchronizedConnection has been destroyed during postponed delivery";
             continue;
         }
 
